# The root URL serves the SPA shell, and that shell hardcodes content-hashed
# asset filenames that change on every deploy. An edge or browser copy that
# outlives a deploy asks for chunk names the new deployment does not have.
#
# History: `max-age=3600, s-maxage=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800` meant
# a day of edge staleness after every release (`cf-cache-status: HIT`,
# `age: 52300`). Pages' default `max-age=0, must-revalidate` fixed that but
# revalidates at origin on every request (`cf-cache-status: EXPIRED`), which
# costs a far-colo round trip each time.
#
# Now: browsers always revalidate (`max-age=0`), the edge may serve a copy for
# 5 minutes and refresh it in the background for 1 more minute. Worst-case
# staleness after a deploy is therefore bounded to about 6 minutes.
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=300, stale-while-revalidate=60

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=300, stale-while-revalidate=60
